# OKF Standards (`conifervision/`)

The vault is an [OKF v0.2](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog/tree/main/okf) knowledge bundle. Spec: [OKF SPEC.md](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog/blob/main/okf/SPEC.md). Domain contract also in `AGENTS.md`.

## Bundle layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `conifervision/index.md` | Root index — **only** `okf_version: "0.2"` in frontmatter |
| `conifervision/log.md` | Chronological history — **no** frontmatter |
| `conifervision/<dir>/index.md` | Progressive disclosure listing — **no** frontmatter |
| `conifervision/**/*.md` (else) | Concept documents |

Concept ID = file path without `.md` (e.g. `methods/local-maxima`).

## Required concept frontmatter

```yaml
type: Method | Concept | Source | Project | Experiment   # REQUIRED (domain types)
title: Human-readable title
description: One-line summary                              # recommended
tags: [tag1, tag2]
status: draft | stable | deprecated                        # OKF lifecycle (not "active")
generated:
  by: agent:ingest/gemini-3.5-flash | human:<name>
  at: 2026-06-09T12:00:00Z
```

Legacy extensions (keep when useful): `updated`, `related_methods`, `source_file`, `authors`, `year`, `replication_status`.

**Status mapping:** `active` → `stable`, `superseded` → `deprecated`, `candidate` → `draft`.

## Provenance (`sources`)

Prefer OKF structured entries on literature-backed concepts:

```yaml
sources:
  - id: popescu-2004
    resource: raw/papers/Seeing_the_Trees_in_the_Forest_Using_Lidar_and_Mul.pdf
    title: Popescu & Wynne (2004) — LiDAR CHM local maxima
    last_modified: 2004-05-01
```

Internal bundle links: `resource: /sources/slug.md` or footnotes keyed by `sources[].id`.

## Links

- **OKF (preferred for new edits):** `[Title](/methods/local-maxima.md)` — bundle-relative, leading `/`
- **Obsidian/Quartz (existing):** `[[methods/local-maxima]]` — keep working; do not mass-convert unless asked

## Progressive disclosure

When adding a concept under a subdirectory:

1. Create `path/to/concept.md` with OKF frontmatter.
2. Add bullet to that directory's `index.md` (title + description).
3. Update root `conifervision/index.md` if it is a top-level entry.
4. Append `conifervision/log.md` on ingest/lint.

## After vault edits

```bash
make okf-lint          # check conformance
make okf-lint FIX=1    # apply safe frontmatter fixes
make build-wiki-docker # verify Quartz still builds
```

Optional OKF graph (reference agent from Google knowledge-catalog): clone `okf/` and run `reference_agent visualize --bundle conifervision`.
